            "role": "assistant",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today (Friday, **July 31, 2026**), the biggest “Azure AI” news is tied to Microsoft’s FY26 Q4 results and the knock-on coverage around Azure’s AI-driven growth:\n\n- **Azure growth is being attributed heavily to AI adoption**, with multiple reports focusing on an earnings-driven surge in Microsoft’s share price and Azure momentum. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/other/azure-ignites-microsoft-stock-ai-fueled-earnings-beat-sparks-9-rally/ar-AA294cLq))  \n- **Microsoft’s official earnings write-up (published July 29, 2026)** emphasizes “Microsoft Cloud and AI strength” in the quarter ending **June 30, 2026**, and includes details on how OpenAI investment impacts were accounted for in results. ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/07/29/microsoft-cloud-and-ai-strength-fuels-fourth-quarter-results-4/))  \n- On the infrastructure side, Microsoft announced it is **expanding Azure AI/HPC infrastructure with AMD** (published **July 20, 2026**), positioning this as part of scaling capacity for how customers build/run AI systems on Azure. ([blogs.microsoft.com](https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/07/20/microsoft-expands-azure-ai-and-hpc-infrastructure-with-amd/))  \n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Azure OpenAI Service**, **Azure AI Foundry/Microsoft Foundry**, **Azure AI Search**, **Content Safety**, etc.), I can narrow this to just the most relevant “today” items and ignore the earnings/stock angle.",
